# ⛔ ICON I/O-TEST SCRATCH — A NET FOR THE UNFIXED PATHS, NOT THE CURE (hq_B 2026-08-30).
# rung36_jcon_io.icn opens tmp1/tmp2 ("w") and rung36_jcon_iobig.icn testio()s tmp3/tmp4, all relative
# to the CWD. ceo removed the accidentally-committed tests/icon/tmp3 (4bd836184) and the next
# test_icon_all_rungs.sh run put it straight back as an untracked file, which handoff_status.sh reads
# as a dirty corpus. ⭐ THE ACTUAL CURE IS THE WRITER, AND IT IS LANDED FOR THE MEASURED PATH:
# test_icon_all_rungs.sh now runs every entry from a scratch cwd with the program passed absolute
# (SCRIP-side commit), so what a test WRITES no longer lands in the source tree. A/B'd: totals
# identical (PASS=262 FAIL=7 BADEXIT=1 XFAIL=27 TOTAL=297) and the corpus stays clean.
# ⛔ THIS PATTERN REMAINS ONLY BECAUSE ~5 SIBLING GRADERS STILL RUN FROM THE CORPUS CWD AND ARE NOT
# YET CONVERTED — test_icon_x64_all_rungs.sh documents its corpus cwd as DELIBERATE ("so relative
# data-file reads resolve exactly as they do under --run"), so each needs its own A/B before moving.
# Do not read this line as the class being closed: it is a net under an unfinished conversion, and
# hq_C is right that an ignore rule left standing alone would silence a symptom while the writer lives.
# ⚠️ Also does NOT untrack tmp1/tmp2/tmp4, still committed test litter (tmp4 = 403,609 bytes of
# generated binary). Removing tracked content is ceo's call, not this seat's — routed.
tests/icon/tmp[0-9]*
# ⛔ FILES THE GRADED PROGRAMS THEMSELVES WRITE (ceo 2026-09-14). These are not build litter and not a
# symptom to be silenced: ASM.sno's own header says "running this writes ASMTEMP into the working directory",
# and the x64 save/module programs write their save files by design -- the suites grade the programs' stdout,
# and the side effect is part of what the program IS. Left untracked they make the corpus tree DIRTY, and a
# dirty corpus makes util_score_row.py REFUSE to land the row (CEO-174: a dirty-tree number describes no
# checkable tree), so a correct measurement silently failed to publish three times in one sitting.
# ⛔ SCOPED BY NAME AND BY DIRECTORY ON PURPOSE: a broad *.out or *.spx would hide real corpus files.
packages/snobol4/gimpel/asmtemp
packages/snobol4/spitbol_x64_tests/*.spx
packages/snobol4/spitbol_x64_tests/module.out
